  "description": "Roamer is a mid-drive cruiser electric bike with 350W or 500W Bafang motor options, torque-sensing pedal assist and dual 48V 14Ah LG batteries. Its step-through frame, upright position and front suspension support everyday cycling. Roamer has no throttle: assistance follows your pedaling effort. What makes Roamer a cruiser electric bike? Roamer combines a step-through frame, upright riding position and 27.5-inch wheels with vintage-inspired styling. Its cruiser layout suits paved beachfront paths, town rides and leisure outings, with a suspension fork and comfort saddle supporting everyday cycling. How does torque-sensing assist follow your effort? A torque sensor measures how hard you pedal and adjusts motor support to match. Roamer's five assist levels let you choose the support for your route, preserving the feel of pedaling a bicycle while reducing the effort needed for starts and hills. Which Bafang mid-drive motor can you choose? Choose a 350W or 500W Bafang mid-drive motor. Power passes through the bicycle's drivetrain and Shimano 7-speed gearing, so you can match the gear to a climb or cruising pace. Both motor options use torque-sensing pedal assistance without a throttle. What do dual batteries add to your daily ride? Two 48V 14Ah LG-cell batteries provide a combined 28Ah capacity and 1,344Wh of nominal energy. The front-and-rear battery arrangement supports longer plans between charges, from commuting to leisure rides, while retaining Roamer's step-through cruiser frame. How can you carry essentials on a cruiser ebike? Roamer includes a rear rack and full fenders for errands and everyday travel. Add a compatible basket or bag for work items and shopping. The 350 lb total payload includes the rider and cargo; the wicker basket shown is optional. How do the tires and brakes support city riding? The 27.5 × 2.1-inch Kenda tires suit paved commuting and leisure routes. Logan hydraulic disc brakes provide braking control, while front suspension cushions broken pavement. Together with seven Shimano gears, these features support changing speeds and gradients on everyday rides.",
